  "composition": {
    "child": "TCIA Pediatric-CT-SEG 2197048C: 11-year-old boy, 140.1 cm, 48.5 kg; contrast CT (IV, portal phase), 0.625 mm, from C7 to below the lesser trochanters, arms raised. Kept: thorax, abdomen, pelvis, spine T1-S5, ribs, sternum, proximal femurs with their open physes; enhanced blood re-assigned to blood.",
    "head": "TotalSegmentator s1082 (69 M), C7/T1 disc up; neck at the child's vertebral scale (x0.77), lengthened 15 % at mid-neck, cranium x0.885 (head circumference 53.5 cm).",
    "arms": "VSD z053 (57 F) right shoulder girdle and arm, mirrored for the left; placed on the child's ribs 2-7, T1-T7 and sternoclavicular joints, let down to hang at rest, x0.88.",
    "legs": "VSD z035 (30 F) right lower extremity (baked anatomical position), mirrored for the left; hung from the child's femoral heads, joined to the child's femur below the trochanters, x0.83, thighs widened to the child's outline.",
    "physes": "cut into the grafted bones: proximal humerus, distal radius and ulna, distal femur, proximal and distal tibia, proximal fibula. Not cut: the distal fibula (it lies against the tibia there in the donor), the small bones of the hands and feet, the centres of the elbow."
  }
